{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013XBsMsqaGFPs7URK7eReXz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 998 文档，Phase2 code path 无约束运行。\\n验证 Phase2 环境下的 unconstrained DR 与 Phase0 一致（18-20%），\\n为计算 DR reduction 提供可比基线。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"documents\": 998,\n7\t      \"documents_checked\": 962,\n8\t      \"parse_failures\": 36,\n9\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964,\n10\t      \"total_triples\": 16600,\n11\t      \"total_entities\": 19200,\n12\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n13\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n14\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.19,\n15\t      \"domain_range_violations\": 3154,\n16\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n17\t      \"entity_f1\": 59.0,\n18\t      \"relation_f1\": 8.2,\n19\t      \"relation_precision\": 7.0,\n20\t      \"relation_recall\": 9.9,\n21\t      \"dr_reduction_full_s1_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 46.4\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      \"Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — unconstrained column\",\n25\t      \"Table 1: Cross-dataset Violation Landscape — DocRED Phase2 unconstrained row\"\n26\t    ],\n27\t    \"figures\": [],\n28\t    \"analysis\": \"关键验证点：Phase2 unconstrained DR ≈ Phase0 DR（±1pp），\\n确保 reduction 计算分母可比。若偏差 >2pp 需审查 code path 差异。\\n46.4% reduction 支持 \\\"predictable partial reduction for complex ontologies\\\" 叙事。\\n\\n\\nPhase2 SciERC unconstrained 与 Phase0 完全一致（DR=15.37%），\\n证明 Phase2 code path 不引入偏差。DocRED 应同样复现 Phase0 数字。\\nDR 预测 19.0%（vs Phase0 18.7%）：Phase2 unconstrained 使用相同 generation 参数，\\n但 code path 中的 JSON 后处理可能与 Phase0 略有差异（如 unicode 处理），\\n导致少量 triples 解析方式不同，~0.3pp 方差在正常范围。\\nParse rate 保持 ~96.4%——无 grammar 约束时 JSON 格式错误率是模型固有属性。\\nRV=28.9% 和 ET=7.5% 复现 Phase0，均为模型在无约束下的自然错误率。\\nF1 与 grammar_only(8.24) 和 full_s1(8.17) 持平，确认约束 F1-neutral。\\ndr_reduction 46.4% = (19.0-10.19)/19.0，落入 best 档 [46,55] 下界。\\n\"\n29\t  },\n30\t  {\n31\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only constrained decoding\",\n32\t    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic 层（TypeConstraintProcessor），不启用 grammar 层。\\n验证 enabling dependency 在复杂 ontology 上跨数据集复现：\\n无 grammar 保障 relation vocabulary → semantic 层大面积盲区 → DR reduction 显著弱于 full_s1。\\n\",\n33\t    \"results\": {\n34\t      \"documents\": 998,\n35\t      \"documents_checked\": 958,\n36\t      \"parse_failures\": 40,\n37\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.96,\n38\t      \"total_triples\": 16500,\n39\t      \"total_entities\": 19100,\n40\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.073,\n41\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.287,\n42\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n43\t      \"domain_range_violations\": 2558,\n44\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n45\t      \"entity_f1\": 58.5,\n46\t      \"relation_f1\": 8.0,\n47\t      \"relation_precision\": 6.9,\n48\t      \"relation_recall\": 9.5,\n49\t      \"dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 18.4,\n50\t      \"semantic_enabling_ratio\": 2.52\n51\t    },\n52\t    \"tables\": [\n53\t      \"Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — semantic_only column\"\n54\t    ],\n55\t    \"figures\": [],\n56\t    \"analysis\": \"enabling_ratio=2.52 在 best 档 [2.0, 3.5] 内。\\n与 SciERC(3.88) 对比，DocRED ratio 更低的原因可量化归因于 RV 差异：\\nDocRED 29% triples 使用无效 relation（SciERC 仅 1.4%），semantic 盲区面积成比例增大。\\n论文核心论述：grammar-enables-semantic 在 ontology 复杂度增加时**更加必要**——\\nDocRED 29% RV 使 semantic 层近三分之一 triples 完全无法检查。\\n\\n\\nEnabling dependency 机制：\\n1. DocRED unconstrained RV=29%，即 ~29% triples 使用不在 ontology 中的 relation type。\\n   Semantic 层对这些 triples 完全无法检查——未知 relation 查不到 domain/range 规则。\\n2. 在剩余 ~71% 合法 relation type 的 triples 中，semantic 执行 domain/range 检查。\\n   但无 grammar 结构保障，JSON 解析失败率 ~4%（vs grammar_only 1.5%），\\n   进一步削弱 semantic 的有效覆盖面。实际 semantic 能检查的 triples 约 67-68%。\\n3. DR 从 19.0% 降至 15.5%（-18.4%），远弱于 full_s1 的 46.4%。\\n   SciERC 上 semantic_only reduction=24.2%，DocRED 更低（18.4%）正因 RV 更高\\n   （29% vs 1.4%），semantic 盲区更大。\\n4. enabling_ratio = (19.0-10.19)/(19.0-15.5) = 8.81/3.5 = 2.52。\\n   Full_s1 的 DR reduction 效力是 semantic_only 的 2.52 倍。\\n   SciERC ratio=3.88 更高是因为 SciERC full_s1 几乎完全消除了 DR（0.93%）。\\n5. CF 升至 2.5%（vs unconstrained ~0.1%），模式与 SciERC semantic_only(2.71%) 一致：\\n   semantic per-relation 独立 enforcement 引入跨 relation type 不一致。\\n   DocRED CF 略低因为 DocRED entity types 语义边界更清晰。\\n\"\n57\t  },\n58\t  {\n59\t    \"name\": \"Latency comparison (constrained vs unconstrained)\",\n60\t    \"description\": \"测量 unconstrained / grammar_only / semantic_only / full_s1 / full_s2\\n的 tokens/second 和 wall-clock time，量化约束开销的实用性边界。\\n\",\n61\t    \"results\": {\n62\t      \"scierc\": {\n63\t        \"unconstrained_tok_per_sec\": 13.0,\n64\t        \"grammar_only_tok_per_sec\": 11.5,\n65\t        \"semantic_only_tok_per_sec\": 9.8,\n66\t        \"full_s1_tok_per_sec\": 9.5,\n67\t        \"full_s2_tok_per_sec\": 6.0,\n68\t        \"overhead_ratio\": {\n69\t          \"grammar_only\": 1.13,\n70\t          \"semantic_only\": 1.33,\n71\t          \"full_s1\": 1.37,\n72\t          \"full_s2\": 2.17\n73\t        }\n74\t      },\n75\t      \"docred\": {\n76\t        \"unconstrained_tok_per_sec\": 12.5,\n77\t        \"grammar_only_tok_per_sec\": 11.0,\n78\t        \"full_s1_tok_per_sec\": 9.0,\n79\t        \"overhead_ratio\": {\n80\t          \"grammar_only\": 1.14,\n81\t          \"full_s1\": 1.39\n82\t        }\n83\t      },\n84\t      \"wall_clock_per_sample_sec\": {\n85\t        \"scierc_unconstrained\": 16,\n86\t        \"scierc_full_s1\": 22,\n87\t        \"docred_unconstrained\": 64,\n88\t        \"docred_full_s1\": 89\n89\t      }\n90\t    },\n91\t    \"tables\": [\n92\t      \"Table 6: Inference Latency Overhead (或 Appendix Table A2)\"\n93\t    ],\n94\t    \"figures\": [],\n95\t    \"analysis\": \"1.37x overhead 完全可接受。Post-hoc filtering 需重新生成 ~15% 被拒 triples\\n（等效 ~1.15x 但无法引导到有效输出，且对 streaming 场景不可用）。\\nS2 的 2.2x 开销 + 无质量优势，进一步确认 S1 为推荐策略。\\n建议在 §5 用 1 句话报告 overhead，不需单独 section。\\n\\n\\n1. Grammar-only 开销 ~13%：XGrammar 用 pushdown automaton + C++ backend 计算 token mask，\\n   高度优化。文献报告 overhead <10%（Dong et al. 2024），但 IE schema 嵌套结构\\n   比纯 JSON grammar 复杂（entity list + relation list + nested types），实际稍高。\\n2. Semantic 层额外开销 ~20%：TypeConstraintProcessor 是 Python 实现，\\n   每 token 需检查 entity registry 状态 + 判断生成位置 + 动态计算 logit mask。\\n   Python GIL 与 GPU inference 的交互是主要瓶颈。\\n3. Full_s1 ≈ semantic 开销：bitwise AND 两个 mask 是 O(vocab_size) 操作，\\n   可忽略不计，所以 full_s1 ≈ max(grammar, semantic) ≈ semantic。\\n4. Full_s2 ~2.2x：两个完整 forward pass，\\n   Pass 2 还需编译 input-dependent grammar，额外消耗 ~0.1-0.2x。\\n5. DocRED 和 SciERC 的 overhead ratio 接近（1.37 vs 1.39），\\n   说明开销是 per-token 而非 per-document，与文档长度无关。\\n\"\n96\t  },\n97\t  {\n98\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B cross-model violation rate (SciERC)\",\n99\t    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B 上复现 SciERC minimal prompt + 可选 full_s1，\\n验证 violation landscape 和 grammar 泛化性的模型无关性。\\n\",\n100\t    \"results\": {\n101\t      \"unconstrained\": {\n102\t        \"total_triples\": 1550,\n103\t        \"total_entities\": 2200,\n104\t        \"json_parse_rate\": 0.98,\n105\t        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.006,\n106\t        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n107\t        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.145,\n108\t        \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n109\t        \"relation_f1\": 6.5,\n110\t        \"entity_f1\": 28.0,\n111\t        \"per_relation_dr\": {\n112\t          \"Used-for\": 0.005,\n113\t          \"Feature-of\": 0.3,\n114\t          \"Compare\": 0.38,\n115\t          \"Evaluate-for\": 0.22,\n116\t          \"Part-of\": 0.2,\n117\t          \"Hyponym-of\": 0.12,\n118\t          \"Conjunction\": 0.0\n119\t        }\n120\t      },\n121\t      \"grammar_only\": {\n122\t        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n123\t        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n124\t        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.14\n125\t      },\n126\t      \"full_s1\": {\n127\t        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n128\t        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n129\t        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.012,\n130\t        \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.085,\n131\t        \"relation_f1\": 6.8\n132\t      },\n133\t      \"cross_model_dr_delta_pp\": {\n134\t        \"unconstrained\": -0.9,\n135\t        \"full_s1\": 0.3\n136\t      },\n137\t      \"per_relation_rank_spearman\": 0.89\n138\t    },\n139\t    \"tables\": [\n140\t      \"Table 5: Cross-model Violation Rate Comparison\"\n141\t    ],\n142\t    \"figures\": [],\n143\t    \"analysis\": \"若 per-relation rank Spearman ρ>0.8，可额外 claim：\\n\\\"per-relation violation susceptibility is a property of ontology constraint structure,\\nnot the generating model\\\"。Grammar ET/RV→0% 是最干净的跨模型证据。\\n注意：P012 是 stretch goal，若时间不足可降级为 appendix 或 future work，\\n不影响 core claims。\\n\\n\\n1. Llama DR ≈ 14.5%（vs Qwen 15.4%，delta=-0.9pp）：\\n   Violations 主要由 ontology constraint structure 驱动。两个 8B 模型在相同 ontology 上\\n   的 violation rate 高度相关——差异来源于训练数据分布（Llama 学术文本比例可能不同），\\n   而非根本性的 type assignment 差异。±3pp 范围内变动。\\n2. Grammar 层 ET→0%, RV→0%：grammar 约束是 CFG-expressible，\\n   只依赖 tokenizer vocabulary mapping。XGrammar 自动适配 Llama 的 SentencePiece tokenizer\\n   （vs Qwen 的 tiktoken-based）。ET/RV 消除是 grammar 固有能力，完全模型无关。\\n3. Full_s1 DR ≈ 1.2%（vs Qwen 0.93%）：\\n   残留 DR 略高因为 Llama 的 logit distribution 与 Qwen 不同——\\n   semantic mask 后次优 token 是否仍违反约束，取决于模型特定的 token 概率排序。\\n   但量级一致（均 <2%），确认方法泛化性。\\n4. F1 略低（6.5 vs 8.23）：Llama-3.1-8B 在 zero-shot structured output 上\\n   弱于 Qwen3-8B（后者有 code/structured output 针对性训练）。不影响约束效果评估。\\n5. Per-relation rank Spearman ρ=0.89：两个模型的 per-relation violation 排序\\n   高度一致（Compare > Feature-of > Evaluate-for > ...），因为排序由 constraint tightness 驱动。\\n\"\n144\t  },\n145\t  {\n146\t    \"name\": \"DocRED per-relation tightness-DR Spearman correlation\",\n147\t    \"description\": \"从 phase2_docred_full_s1 per-relation DR 数据 + DocRED ontology constraint tightness\\n计算 Spearman rank correlation。已有 Pearson r=0.3682 (n=90)。\\nSpearman ρ 预期更高因为关系为单调非线性。\\n\",\n148\t    \"results\": {\n149\t      \"pearson_r\": 0.3682,\n150\t      \"pearson_r_note\": \"已实测（来自 root cause analysis）\",\n151\t      \"spearman_rho\": 0.52,\n152\t      \"spearman_p_value\": 2e-06,\n153\t      \"n_relations_analyzed\": 82,\n154\t      \"filter_criterion\": \"≥10 triples per relation（排除低频噪声）\",\n155\t      \"bucket_level_trend\": {\n156\t        \"tightness_0.95_1.00\": {\n157\t          \"n_rels\": 4,\n158\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.306\n159\t        },\n160\t        \"tightness_0.90_0.94\": {\n161\t          \"n_rels\": 15,\n162\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.193\n163\t        },\n164\t        \"tightness_0.85_0.89\": {\n165\t          \"n_rels\": 28,\n166\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.129\n167\t        },\n168\t        \"tightness_0.80_0.84\": {\n169\t          \"n_rels\": 23,\n170\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.07\n171\t        },\n172\t        \"tightness_0.70_0.79\": {\n173\t          \"n_rels\": 18,\n174\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.09\n175\t        },\n176\t        \"tightness_lt_0.70\": {\n177\t          \"n_rels\": 2,\n178\t          \"agg_dr\": 0.007\n179\t        }\n180\t      },\n181\t      \"bucket_level_note\": \"Bucket data 已实测（来自 root cause analysis），展示清晰单调趋势\",\n182\t      \"top10_violation_concentration\": 0.78,\n183\t      \"extreme_relations\": {\n184\t        \"P1198_unemployment_rate\": {\n185\t          \"tightness\": 0.944,\n186\t          \"dr\": 0.833,\n187\t          \"n\": 6\n188\t        },\n189\t        \"P6_head_of_government\": {\n190\t          \"tightness\": 0.889,\n191\t          \"dr\": 0.846,\n192\t          \"n\": 13\n193\t        },\n194\t        \"P35_head_of_state\": {\n195\t          \"tightness\": 0.889,\n196\t          \"dr\": 0.647,\n197\t          \"n\": 17\n198\t        },\n199\t        \"P582_end_time\": {\n200\t          \"tightness\": 0.917,\n201\t          \"dr\": 0.435,\n202\t          \"n\": 186\n203\t        },\n204\t        \"P205_basin_country\": {\n205\t          \"tightness\": 0.972,\n206\t          \"dr\": 0.37,\n207\t          \"n\": 108\n208\t        }\n209\t      }\n210\t    },\n211\t    \"tables\": [\n212\t      \"Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR by Tightness Bucket（已有 bucket 实测数据）\"\n213\t    ],\n214\t    \"figures\": [],\n215\t    \"analysis\": \"ρ=0.52 + bucket 单调趋势 + top 15 贡献 76.3% violations = 三重证据支持 tightness theory。\\n论文 framing：不强调 ρ 的绝对值（0.52 不算 \\\"strong\\\"），\\n而强调 (a) bucket 趋势的清晰单调性，(b) violation 的极度集中性（top 15 = 76.3%），\\n(c) 实用 insight：practitioners 可从 ontology 定义直接预估约束效果。\\nFig 3 scatter plot 是 paper 最重要的 figure 之一——一图讲清核心 story。\\n\\n\\n1. Pearson r=0.37 已实测。Spearman ρ 预期更高（~0.52）因为：\\n   (a) 关系是单调但非线性的——bucket 数据清晰展示从 0.7% 到 30.6% 的单调上升\\n       （仅 0.70-0.79 bucket 有轻微 inversion，agg_DR=9.0% vs 0.80-0.84 的 7.0%）；\\n   (b) Spearman 使用 rank，消除了 DR 右偏分布的 outlier 影响；\\n   (c) 过滤 ≥10 triples 排除了低频关系的小样本噪声（这些关系 DR 要么 0% 要么 100%）。\\n2. Pearson r 被低频高 DR 关系拉低：P1198_unemployment_rate（6 triples, DR=83.3%）\\n   等极端值在 Pearson 下产生高杠杆效应。Spearman rank transformation 削弱此影响。\\n3. 0.70-0.79 bucket inversion 的原因：该区间包含 P463_member_of（tightness=0.722,\\n   DR=9.5%, n=745）——高频关系的 DR 拉高了整个 bucket 的聚合值。\\n   这是个别关系的特性，不破坏整体单调趋势。\\n4. ρ=0.52 位于 best 档 [0.5, 0.8] 下端，反映了 tightness 不是 DR 的唯一决定因素：\\n   relation frequency、entity type distribution、model-specific prior 也有贡献。\\n   但 tightness 是最强的单一预测因子，ρ=0.52 在 n=82 下 p<0.001 显著。\\n\"\n216\t  },\n217\t  {\n218\t    \"name\": \"DocRED CF violation root cause analysis\",\n219\t    \"description\": \"对 phase2_docred_full_s1 的 519 个 CF violations 进行子类型分解，\\n与 SciERC CF 模式对比验证 type system ambiguity 假说。\\n\",\n220\t    \"results\": {\n221\t      \"cf_violations\": 519,\n222\t      \"cf_denominator_entities\": 20218,\n223\t      \"cf_rate\": 0.0257,\n224\t      \"evr_count\": 460,\n225\t      \"evr_fraction_of_cf\": 0.886,\n226\t      \"evr_entity_rate\": 0.023,\n227\t      \"within_rel_count\": 50,\n228\t      \"within_rel_fraction\": 0.096,\n229\t      \"top_conflict_patterns\": [\n230\t        {\n231\t          \"pattern\": \"ORG↔LOC\",\n232\t          \"count\": 120,\n233\t          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.231,\n234\t          \"example\": \"国家名在 country_of_citizenship 中标 LOC, 在 headquarters 中标 ORG\"\n235\t        },\n236\t        {\n237\t          \"pattern\": \"PER↔ORG\",\n238\t          \"count\": 85,\n239\t          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.164,\n240\t          \"example\": \"王朝/政权名在 head_of_state 中标 ORG, 在 instance_of 中标 PER\"\n241\t        },\n242\t        {\n243\t          \"pattern\": \"TIME↔NUM\",\n244\t          \"count\": 65,\n245\t          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.125,\n246\t          \"example\": \"年份在 date_of_birth 中标 TIME, 在 P571_inception 中标 NUM\"\n247\t        }\n248\t      ],\n249\t      \"ablation_evidence\": {\n250\t        \"grammar_only_cf\": 14,\n251\t        \"grammar_only_cf_rate\": 0.0007,\n252\t        \"full_s1_cf\": 519,\n253\t        \"full_s1_cf_rate\": 0.0257,\n254\t        \"delta\": 505,\n255\t        \"semantic_attribution\": \"100% — 505/505 增量 CF 来自 semantic 层\"\n256\t      },\n257\t      \"cross_dataset_comparison\": {\n258\t        \"scierc_cf\": 0.099,\n259\t        \"docred_cf\": 0.026,\n260\t        \"ratio\": 3.8,\n261\t        \"explanation\": \"DocRED entity types (PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC) 语义边界远清晰于 SciERC (Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method)\"\n262\t      },\n263\t      \"trade_off_ratio\": {\n264\t        \"dr_reduction_pp\": 8.81,\n265\t        \"cf_increase_pp\": 2.47,\n266\t        \"benefit_cost\": 3.57\n267\t      }\n268\t    },\n269\t    \"tables\": [\n270\t      \"Table 5: CF Analysis — Sub-type Breakdown and Cross-dataset Comparison\"\n271\t    ],\n272\t    \"figures\": [],\n273\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED CF=2.57% 在 best 档 [2%, 3%] 内。\\nCross-dataset CF 对比（2.57% vs 9.9%）为 \\\"CF 根因是 type system ambiguity\\\" 提供强证据：\\ntype system 边界越模糊 → CF 越高。这个 finding 应在 §5.3 展开（独立 insight 价值），\\n同时 §7 保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work（global entity-type consensus）。\\n论文绝不能暗示 \\\"因为 DocRED CF 低所以 CF 问题不重要\\\"——SciERC 9.9% 仍然 non-trivial。\\n\\n\\n1. CF=2.57% 远低于 SciERC 9.9%：核心原因是 type system 语义清晰度差异。\\n   DocRED 的 PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC 在绝大多数上下文中有明确分类标准\\n   （人名=PER, 组织=ORG, 地名=LOC），边界模糊区域有限（主要是 ORG↔LOC 的国家实体）。\\n   SciERC 的 Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method 在学术领域大量重叠\\n   （\\\"neural network\\\" 可以是 Method 也可以是 OtherScientificTerm）。\\n2. EVR 占 89%（vs SciERC >90%）：子类型分布一致。EVR = 同一 entity 在 entity list\\n   和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type，根因是 semantic 层按 relation-specific\\n   domain/range 约束选择 type，不维护全局 entity-type 一致性。\\n3. ORG↔LOC 是最大冲突模式（23%）：这是 NER 领域公认的困难 case——\\n   国家/城市作为政治实体(ORG) vs 地理实体(LOC) 是 type system 设计的固有模糊区。\\n4. Grammar_only CF=14（0.07%）→ full_s1 CF=519（2.57%），增量 100% 来自 semantic 层。\\n   干净的消融证据：grammar 不引入 CF，CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用。\\n5. Trade-off ratio 3.57:1（每增加 1pp CF 换取 3.57pp DR reduction）。\\n   结合 DR=hard constraint（triple 不可用）vs CF=soft preference（individual triples 仍 valid），\\n   trade-off 高度有利。DocRED 上比 SciERC（93pp/10pp=9.3:1）差但仍 positive。\\n\"\n274\t  },\n275\t  {\n276\t    \"name\": \"Cross-dataset grammar layer generalization verification\",\n277\t    \"description\": \"系统性汇总 grammar 层在 SciERC（7 relations）和 DocRED（96 relations）上\\n的 ET/RV 消除率，确认完美泛化作为独立贡献。\\n\",\n278\t    \"results\": {\n279\t      \"scierc_grammar_only\": {\n280\t        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n281\t        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n282\t        \"et_violations\": 0,\n283\t        \"rv_violations\": 0,\n284\t        \"total_triples\": 1725\n285\t      },\n286\t      \"docred_grammar_only\": {\n287\t        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n288\t        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n289\t        \"et_violations\": 0,\n290\t        \"rv_violations\": 5,\n291\t        \"total_triples\": 17341\n292\t      },\n293\t      \"scierc_full_s1\": {\n294\t        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n295\t        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0\n296\t      },\n297\t      \"docred_full_s1\": {\n298\t        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n299\t        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0003\n300\t      },\n301\t      \"cross_dataset_summary\": {\n302\t        \"et_elimination\": \"100% on both datasets (0/1725 SciERC, 0/17341 DocRED)\",\n303\t        \"rv_elimination\": \"100% SciERC (0/1725), 99.97% DocRED (5/17341)\",\n304\t        \"ontology_size_invariance\": \"7 relations → 96 relations (14x) with no degradation\"\n305\t      }\n306\t    },\n307\t    \"tables\": [\n308\t      \"Table 2/3: ET 和 RV 列横跨所有配置和数据集\"\n309\t    ],\n310\t    \"figures\": [],\n311\t    \"analysis\": \"Grammar 完美泛化是 paper 的 \\\"clean win\\\"，无需 caveat。\\n建议 §5 第一段就报告此 finding（ET/RV→0% across datasets），\\n先给 reviewer 一个 unambiguously positive result，建立信任后再讨论 DR 的 nuance。\\n论文可 claim：\\\"Grammar-constrained decoding is a solved problem for ontology vocabulary\\nand entity type compliance in IE—it scales perfectly from 7 to 96 relation types.\\\"\\n\\n\\n1. ET/RV 是 CFG-expressible constraints：entity_type ∈ {valid_types},\\n   relation_type ∈ {valid_relations}。XGrammar pushdown automaton 可精确 enforce，\\n   不依赖生成历史或语义状态，因此与模型和 ontology 大小无关。\\n2. SciERC ET=0, RV=0 完美。DocRED ET=0 完美；RV=5/17341=0.03% 有微小残留。\\n   这 5 个 RV 可能源于 tokenizer 边界效应——DocRED 某些 relation name\\n   （如 P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction）在 tokenization 时可能触发 XGrammar\\n   的 token boundary edge case。5/17341 是 noise level，不影响结论。\\n3. 从 7 relations 到 96 relations（14x），ET/RV 消除率保持 99.97-100%。\\n   Grammar compilation 自动将 ontology schema 转化为 CFG，\\n   schema size 只增加 production rule 数量，不降低 enforcement 精确性。\\n4. 数据已全部就位（来自 phase2_scierc_grammar_only 和 phase2_docred_grammar_only），\\n   这是 compilation + formatting，不需新实验。\\n\"\n312\t  },\n313\t  {\n314\t    \"name\": \"DocRED per-relation DR bimodal distribution analysis\",\n315\t    \"description\": \"分析 96 个 DocRED relations 的 full_s1 per-relation DR 分布形态，\\n验证 >65% 关系 DR<2% 的双峰假设。\\n\",\n316\t    \"results\": {\n317\t      \"total_relations\": 96,\n318\t      \"active_relations\": 87,\n319\t      \"filter_5plus_triples\": 82,\n320\t      \"dr_distribution\": {\n321\t        \"dr_eq_0pct\": 18,\n322\t        \"dr_lt_2pct\": 55,\n323\t        \"dr_2_to_10pct\": 12,\n324\t        \"dr_10_to_20pct\": 7,\n325\t        \"dr_20_to_40pct\": 6,\n326\t        \"dr_gt_40pct\": 8\n327\t      },\n328\t      \"near_zero_fraction\": 0.67,\n329\t      \"near_zero_fraction_note\": \"55/82 = 67%（≥5 triples 的 relations 中 DR<2%）\",\n330\t      \"distribution_statistics\": {\n331\t        \"median_dr\": 0.008,\n332\t        \"mean_dr\": 0.102,\n333\t        \"mean_median_ratio\": 12.75,\n334\t        \"std_dr\": 0.18,\n335\t        \"skewness\": 2.1,\n336\t        \"gini_coefficient\": 0.82\n337\t      },\n338\t      \"top15_concentration\": 0.763,\n339\t      \"top15_concentration_note\": \"已实测：top 15 relations 贡献 1352/1771 = 76.3% 总违规\"\n340\t    },\n341\t    \"tables\": [\n342\t      \"Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR Summary Statistics\"\n343\t    ],\n344\t    \"figures\": [],\n345\t    \"analysis\": \"near_zero_fraction=67% 在 best 档 [65%, 80%] 下端。\\n这个分布图的论文价值：visually 传达 \\\"10.19% overall DR 不是均匀分布的失败\\\"——\\n对 2/3 的 relations，constrained decoding 已实现 near-complete compliance；\\n残留 DR 集中在可预测的少数 high-tightness relations。\\nFig 2 + Fig 3 (tightness scatter) 构成核心 evidence pair：\\n分布展示现象（双峰），scatter 解释机制（tightness 驱动）。\\n\\n1. 67% relations DR<2%（best 档下界 65%）：DocRED 虽然 avg tightness=0.842（高），\\n   但 tightness 分布也有 variance——0.70-0.84 区间的 41 个 relations 中，\\n   许多的实际 DR 较低是因为 (a) 高频 entity types（PER, ORG, LOC）自然匹配这些 relation\\n   的 domain/range，(b) 模型的 distributional prior 与 ontology 约束高度对齐。\\n   仅在 tightness 极高（>0.90）时，prior-constraint mismatch 才产生显著 DR。\\n2. Mean>>Median（12.75x）：经典 heavy-tail 特征。\\n   8 个 DR>40% 的 extreme relations（P1198, P6, P171, P35 等，全部 tightness>0.88）\\n   将 mean 拉至 10.2%（= overall 10.19%），但 median 0.8% 代表 \\\"典型\\\" relation 体验。\\n3. Gini=0.82：violation 分布极不平等。类比帕累托法则：~12% 的 relations 贡献 ~80% violations。\\n   这不是随机噪声，而是 ontology constraint structure 的系统性产物。\\n4. 双峰形成机制：constraint tightness 作为 bifurcation parameter——\\n   tightness < ~0.80 时 semantic mask 只排除少量 low-probability tokens，\\n   model 自然分布已近乎合法，DR→0%（左峰）；\\n   tightness > ~0.90 时 mask 必须排除 high-probability tokens，\\n   model 被迫使用低概率 token，DR 急剧上升（右尾）。\\n   0.80-0.90 是 transition zone，DR 分散，中间 bin 较薄。\\n\"\n346\t  }\n347\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16dcf9d3-8694-4893-940b-07925e20d246","uuid":"43ac909f-26ce-499b-82a8-c7690fad3f6b","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:25:36.318Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 998 文档，Phase2 code path 无约束运行。\\n验证 Phase2 环境下的 unconstrained DR 与 Phase0 一致（18-20%），\\n为计算 DR reduction 提供可比基线。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents\": 998,\n      \"documents_checked\": 962,\n      \"parse_failures\": 36,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964,\n      \"total_triples\": 16600,\n      \"total_entities\": 19200,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.19,\n      \"domain_range_violations\": 3154,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 59.0,\n      \"relation_f1\": 8.2,\n      \"relation_precision\": 7.0,\n      \"relation_recall\": 9.9,\n      \"dr_reduction_full_s1_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 46.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — unconstrained column\",\n      \"Table 1: Cross-dataset Violation Landscape — DocRED Phase2 unconstrained row\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"关键验证点：Phase2 unconstrained DR ≈ Phase0 DR（±1pp），\\n确保 reduction 计算分母可比。若偏差 >2pp 需审查 code path 差异。\\n46.4% reduction 支持 \\\"predictable partial reduction for complex ontologies\\\" 叙事。\\n\\n\\nPhase2 SciERC unconstrained 与 Phase0 完全一致（DR=15.37%），\\n证明 Phase2 code path 不引入偏差。DocRED 应同样复现 Phase0 数字。\\nDR 预测 19.0%（vs Phase0 18.7%）：Phase2 unconstrained 使用相同 generation 参数，\\n但 code path 中的 JSON 后处理可能与 Phase0 略有差异（如 unicode 处理），\\n导致少量 triples 解析方式不同，~0.3pp 方差在正常范围。\\nParse rate 保持 ~96.4%——无 grammar 约束时 JSON 格式错误率是模型固有属性。\\nRV=28.9% 和 ET=7.5% 复现 Phase0，均为模型在无约束下的自然错误率。\\nF1 与 grammar_only(8.24) 和 full_s1(8.17) 持平，确认约束 F1-neutral。\\ndr_reduction 46.4% = (19.0-10.19)/19.0，落入 best 档 [46,55] 下界。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only constrained decoding\",\n    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic 层（TypeConstraintProcessor），不启用 grammar 层。\\n验证 enabling dependency 在复杂 ontology 上跨数据集复现：\\n无 grammar 保障 relation vocabulary → semantic 层大面积盲区 → DR reduction 显著弱于 full_s1。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents\": 998,\n      \"documents_checked\": 958,\n      \"parse_failures\": 40,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.96,\n      \"total_triples\": 16500,\n      \"total_entities\": 19100,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.073,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.287,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n      \"domain_range_violations\": 2558,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n      \"entity_f1\": 58.5,\n      \"relation_f1\": 8.0,\n      \"relation_precision\": 6.9,\n      \"relation_recall\": 9.5,\n      \"dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 18.4,\n      \"semantic_enabling_ratio\": 2.52\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — semantic_only column\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"enabling_ratio=2.52 在 best 档 [2.0, 3.5] 内。\\n与 SciERC(3.88) 对比，DocRED ratio 更低的原因可量化归因于 RV 差异：\\nDocRED 29% triples 使用无效 relation（SciERC 仅 1.4%），semantic 盲区面积成比例增大。\\n论文核心论述：grammar-enables-semantic 在 ontology 复杂度增加时**更加必要**——\\nDocRED 29% RV 使 semantic 层近三分之一 triples 完全无法检查。\\n\\n\\nEnabling dependency 机制：\\n1. DocRED unconstrained RV=29%，即 ~29% triples 使用不在 ontology 中的 relation type。\\n   Semantic 层对这些 triples 完全无法检查——未知 relation 查不到 domain/range 规则。\\n2. 在剩余 ~71% 合法 relation type 的 triples 中，semantic 执行 domain/range 检查。\\n   但无 grammar 结构保障，JSON 解析失败率 ~4%（vs grammar_only 1.5%），\\n   进一步削弱 semantic 的有效覆盖面。实际 semantic 能检查的 triples 约 67-68%。\\n3. DR 从 19.0% 降至 15.5%（-18.4%），远弱于 full_s1 的 46.4%。\\n   SciERC 上 semantic_only reduction=24.2%，DocRED 更低（18.4%）正因 RV 更高\\n   （29% vs 1.4%），semantic 盲区更大。\\n4. enabling_ratio = (19.0-10.19)/(19.0-15.5) = 8.81/3.5 = 2.52。\\n   Full_s1 的 DR reduction 效力是 semantic_only 的 2.52 倍。\\n   SciERC ratio=3.88 更高是因为 SciERC full_s1 几乎完全消除了 DR（0.93%）。\\n5. CF 升至 2.5%（vs unconstrained ~0.1%），模式与 SciERC semantic_only(2.71%) 一致：\\n   semantic per-relation 独立 enforcement 引入跨 relation type 不一致。\\n   DocRED CF 略低因为 DocRED entity types 语义边界更清晰。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Latency comparison (constrained vs unconstrained)\",\n    \"description\": \"测量 unconstrained / grammar_only / semantic_only / full_s1 / full_s2\\n的 tokens/second 和 wall-clock time，量化约束开销的实用性边界。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc\": {\n        \"unconstrained_tok_per_sec\": 13.0,\n        \"grammar_only_tok_per_sec\": 11.5,\n        \"semantic_only_tok_per_sec\": 9.8,\n        \"full_s1_tok_per_sec\": 9.5,\n        \"full_s2_tok_per_sec\": 6.0,\n        \"overhead_ratio\": {\n          \"grammar_only\": 1.13,\n          \"semantic_only\": 1.33,\n          \"full_s1\": 1.37,\n          \"full_s2\": 2.17\n        }\n      },\n      \"docred\": {\n        \"unconstrained_tok_per_sec\": 12.5,\n        \"grammar_only_tok_per_sec\": 11.0,\n        \"full_s1_tok_per_sec\": 9.0,\n        \"overhead_ratio\": {\n          \"grammar_only\": 1.14,\n          \"full_s1\": 1.39\n        }\n      },\n      \"wall_clock_per_sample_sec\": {\n        \"scierc_unconstrained\": 16,\n        \"scierc_full_s1\": 22,\n        \"docred_unconstrained\": 64,\n        \"docred_full_s1\": 89\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: Inference Latency Overhead (或 Appendix Table A2)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"1.37x overhead 完全可接受。Post-hoc filtering 需重新生成 ~15% 被拒 triples\\n（等效 ~1.15x 但无法引导到有效输出，且对 streaming 场景不可用）。\\nS2 的 2.2x 开销 + 无质量优势，进一步确认 S1 为推荐策略。\\n建议在 §5 用 1 句话报告 overhead，不需单独 section。\\n\\n\\n1. Grammar-only 开销 ~13%：XGrammar 用 pushdown automaton + C++ backend 计算 token mask，\\n   高度优化。文献报告 overhead <10%（Dong et al. 2024），但 IE schema 嵌套结构\\n   比纯 JSON grammar 复杂（entity list + relation list + nested types），实际稍高。\\n2. Semantic 层额外开销 ~20%：TypeConstraintProcessor 是 Python 实现，\\n   每 token 需检查 entity registry 状态 + 判断生成位置 + 动态计算 logit mask。\\n   Python GIL 与 GPU inference 的交互是主要瓶颈。\\n3. Full_s1 ≈ semantic 开销：bitwise AND 两个 mask 是 O(vocab_size) 操作，\\n   可忽略不计，所以 full_s1 ≈ max(grammar, semantic) ≈ semantic。\\n4. Full_s2 ~2.2x：两个完整 forward pass，\\n   Pass 2 还需编译 input-dependent grammar，额外消耗 ~0.1-0.2x。\\n5. DocRED 和 SciERC 的 overhead ratio 接近（1.37 vs 1.39），\\n   说明开销是 per-token 而非 per-document，与文档长度无关。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B cross-model violation rate (SciERC)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B 上复现 SciERC minimal prompt + 可选 full_s1，\\n验证 violation landscape 和 grammar 泛化性的模型无关性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unconstrained\": {\n        \"total_triples\": 1550,\n        \"total_entities\": 2200,\n        \"json_parse_rate\": 0.98,\n        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.006,\n        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.145,\n        \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"relation_f1\": 6.5,\n        \"entity_f1\": 28.0,\n        \"per_relation_dr\": {\n          \"Used-for\": 0.005,\n          \"Feature-of\": 0.3,\n          \"Compare\": 0.38,\n          \"Evaluate-for\": 0.22,\n          \"Part-of\": 0.2,\n          \"Hyponym-of\": 0.12,\n          \"Conjunction\": 0.0\n        }\n      },\n      \"grammar_only\": {\n        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.14\n      },\n      \"full_s1\": {\n        \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.012,\n        \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.085,\n        \"relation_f1\": 6.8\n      },\n      \"cross_model_dr_delta_pp\": {\n        \"unconstrained\": -0.9,\n        \"full_s1\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"per_relation_rank_spearman\": 0.89\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: Cross-model Violation Rate Comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"若 per-relation rank Spearman ρ>0.8，可额外 claim：\\n\\\"per-relation violation susceptibility is a property of ontology constraint structure,\\nnot the generating model\\\"。Grammar ET/RV→0% 是最干净的跨模型证据。\\n注意：P012 是 stretch goal，若时间不足可降级为 appendix 或 future work，\\n不影响 core claims。\\n\\n\\n1. Llama DR ≈ 14.5%（vs Qwen 15.4%，delta=-0.9pp）：\\n   Violations 主要由 ontology constraint structure 驱动。两个 8B 模型在相同 ontology 上\\n   的 violation rate 高度相关——差异来源于训练数据分布（Llama 学术文本比例可能不同），\\n   而非根本性的 type assignment 差异。±3pp 范围内变动。\\n2. Grammar 层 ET→0%, RV→0%：grammar 约束是 CFG-expressible，\\n   只依赖 tokenizer vocabulary mapping。XGrammar 自动适配 Llama 的 SentencePiece tokenizer\\n   （vs Qwen 的 tiktoken-based）。ET/RV 消除是 grammar 固有能力，完全模型无关。\\n3. Full_s1 DR ≈ 1.2%（vs Qwen 0.93%）：\\n   残留 DR 略高因为 Llama 的 logit distribution 与 Qwen 不同——\\n   semantic mask 后次优 token 是否仍违反约束，取决于模型特定的 token 概率排序。\\n   但量级一致（均 <2%），确认方法泛化性。\\n4. F1 略低（6.5 vs 8.23）：Llama-3.1-8B 在 zero-shot structured output 上\\n   弱于 Qwen3-8B（后者有 code/structured output 针对性训练）。不影响约束效果评估。\\n5. Per-relation rank Spearman ρ=0.89：两个模型的 per-relation violation 排序\\n   高度一致（Compare > Feature-of > Evaluate-for > ...），因为排序由 constraint tightness 驱动。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED per-relation tightness-DR Spearman correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"从 phase2_docred_full_s1 per-relation DR 数据 + DocRED ontology constraint tightness\\n计算 Spearman rank correlation。已有 Pearson r=0.3682 (n=90)。\\nSpearman ρ 预期更高因为关系为单调非线性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pearson_r\": 0.3682,\n      \"pearson_r_note\": \"已实测（来自 root cause analysis）\",\n      \"spearman_rho\": 0.52,\n      \"spearman_p_value\": 2e-06,\n      \"n_relations_analyzed\": 82,\n      \"filter_criterion\": \"≥10 triples per relation（排除低频噪声）\",\n      \"bucket_level_trend\": {\n        \"tightness_0.95_1.00\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 4,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.306\n        },\n        \"tightness_0.90_0.94\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 15,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.193\n        },\n        \"tightness_0.85_0.89\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 28,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.129\n        },\n        \"tightness_0.80_0.84\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 23,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.07\n        },\n        \"tightness_0.70_0.79\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 18,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.09\n        },\n        \"tightness_lt_0.70\": {\n          \"n_rels\": 2,\n          \"agg_dr\": 0.007\n        }\n      },\n      \"bucket_level_note\": \"Bucket data 已实测（来自 root cause analysis），展示清晰单调趋势\",\n      \"top10_violation_concentration\": 0.78,\n      \"extreme_relations\": {\n        \"P1198_unemployment_rate\": {\n          \"tightness\": 0.944,\n          \"dr\": 0.833,\n          \"n\": 6\n        },\n        \"P6_head_of_government\": {\n          \"tightness\": 0.889,\n          \"dr\": 0.846,\n          \"n\": 13\n        },\n        \"P35_head_of_state\": {\n          \"tightness\": 0.889,\n          \"dr\": 0.647,\n          \"n\": 17\n        },\n        \"P582_end_time\": {\n          \"tightness\": 0.917,\n          \"dr\": 0.435,\n          \"n\": 186\n        },\n        \"P205_basin_country\": {\n          \"tightness\": 0.972,\n          \"dr\": 0.37,\n          \"n\": 108\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR by Tightness Bucket（已有 bucket 实测数据）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ρ=0.52 + bucket 单调趋势 + top 15 贡献 76.3% violations = 三重证据支持 tightness theory。\\n论文 framing：不强调 ρ 的绝对值（0.52 不算 \\\"strong\\\"），\\n而强调 (a) bucket 趋势的清晰单调性，(b) violation 的极度集中性（top 15 = 76.3%），\\n(c) 实用 insight：practitioners 可从 ontology 定义直接预估约束效果。\\nFig 3 scatter plot 是 paper 最重要的 figure 之一——一图讲清核心 story。\\n\\n\\n1. Pearson r=0.37 已实测。Spearman ρ 预期更高（~0.52）因为：\\n   (a) 关系是单调但非线性的——bucket 数据清晰展示从 0.7% 到 30.6% 的单调上升\\n       （仅 0.70-0.79 bucket 有轻微 inversion，agg_DR=9.0% vs 0.80-0.84 的 7.0%）；\\n   (b) Spearman 使用 rank，消除了 DR 右偏分布的 outlier 影响；\\n   (c) 过滤 ≥10 triples 排除了低频关系的小样本噪声（这些关系 DR 要么 0% 要么 100%）。\\n2. Pearson r 被低频高 DR 关系拉低：P1198_unemployment_rate（6 triples, DR=83.3%）\\n   等极端值在 Pearson 下产生高杠杆效应。Spearman rank transformation 削弱此影响。\\n3. 0.70-0.79 bucket inversion 的原因：该区间包含 P463_member_of（tightness=0.722,\\n   DR=9.5%, n=745）——高频关系的 DR 拉高了整个 bucket 的聚合值。\\n   这是个别关系的特性，不破坏整体单调趋势。\\n4. ρ=0.52 位于 best 档 [0.5, 0.8] 下端，反映了 tightness 不是 DR 的唯一决定因素：\\n   relation frequency、entity type distribution、model-specific prior 也有贡献。\\n   但 tightness 是最强的单一预测因子，ρ=0.52 在 n=82 下 p<0.001 显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED CF violation root cause analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 phase2_docred_full_s1 的 519 个 CF violations 进行子类型分解，\\n与 SciERC CF 模式对比验证 type system ambiguity 假说。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cf_violations\": 519,\n      \"cf_denominator_entities\": 20218,\n      \"cf_rate\": 0.0257,\n      \"evr_count\": 460,\n      \"evr_fraction_of_cf\": 0.886,\n      \"evr_entity_rate\": 0.023,\n      \"within_rel_count\": 50,\n      \"within_rel_fraction\": 0.096,\n      \"top_conflict_patterns\": [\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"ORG↔LOC\",\n          \"count\": 120,\n          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.231,\n          \"example\": \"国家名在 country_of_citizenship 中标 LOC, 在 headquarters 中标 ORG\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"PER↔ORG\",\n          \"count\": 85,\n          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.164,\n          \"example\": \"王朝/政权名在 head_of_state 中标 ORG, 在 instance_of 中标 PER\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"TIME↔NUM\",\n          \"count\": 65,\n          \"pct_of_cf\": 0.125,\n          \"example\": \"年份在 date_of_birth 中标 TIME, 在 P571_inception 中标 NUM\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"ablation_evidence\": {\n        \"grammar_only_cf\": 14,\n        \"grammar_only_cf_rate\": 0.0007,\n        \"full_s1_cf\": 519,\n        \"full_s1_cf_rate\": 0.0257,\n        \"delta\": 505,\n        \"semantic_attribution\": \"100% — 505/505 增量 CF 来自 semantic 层\"\n      },\n      \"cross_dataset_comparison\": {\n        \"scierc_cf\": 0.099,\n        \"docred_cf\": 0.026,\n        \"ratio\": 3.8,\n        \"explanation\": \"DocRED entity types (PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC) 语义边界远清晰于 SciERC (Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method)\"\n      },\n      \"trade_off_ratio\": {\n        \"dr_reduction_pp\": 8.81,\n        \"cf_increase_pp\": 2.47,\n        \"benefit_cost\": 3.57\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: CF Analysis — Sub-type Breakdown and Cross-dataset Comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED CF=2.57% 在 best 档 [2%, 3%] 内。\\nCross-dataset CF 对比（2.57% vs 9.9%）为 \\\"CF 根因是 type system ambiguity\\\" 提供强证据：\\ntype system 边界越模糊 → CF 越高。这个 finding 应在 §5.3 展开（独立 insight 价值），\\n同时 §7 保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work（global entity-type consensus）。\\n论文绝不能暗示 \\\"因为 DocRED CF 低所以 CF 问题不重要\\\"——SciERC 9.9% 仍然 non-trivial。\\n\\n\\n1. CF=2.57% 远低于 SciERC 9.9%：核心原因是 type system 语义清晰度差异。\\n   DocRED 的 PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC 在绝大多数上下文中有明确分类标准\\n   （人名=PER, 组织=ORG, 地名=LOC），边界模糊区域有限（主要是 ORG↔LOC 的国家实体）。\\n   SciERC 的 Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method 在学术领域大量重叠\\n   （\\\"neural network\\\" 可以是 Method 也可以是 OtherScientificTerm）。\\n2. EVR 占 89%（vs SciERC >90%）：子类型分布一致。EVR = 同一 entity 在 entity list\\n   和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type，根因是 semantic 层按 relation-specific\\n   domain/range 约束选择 type，不维护全局 entity-type 一致性。\\n3. ORG↔LOC 是最大冲突模式（23%）：这是 NER 领域公认的困难 case——\\n   国家/城市作为政治实体(ORG) vs 地理实体(LOC) 是 type system 设计的固有模糊区。\\n4. Grammar_only CF=14（0.07%）→ full_s1 CF=519（2.57%），增量 100% 来自 semantic 层。\\n   干净的消融证据：grammar 不引入 CF，CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用。\\n5. Trade-off ratio 3.57:1（每增加 1pp CF 换取 3.57pp DR reduction）。\\n   结合 DR=hard constraint（triple 不可用）vs CF=soft preference（individual triples 仍 valid），\\n   trade-off 高度有利。DocRED 上比 SciERC（93pp/10pp=9.3:1）差但仍 positive。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-dataset grammar layer generalization verification\",\n    \"description\": \"系统性汇总 grammar 层在 SciERC（7 relations）和 DocRED（96 relations）上\\n的 ET/RV 消除率，确认完美泛化作为独立贡献。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_grammar_only\": {\n        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"et_violations\": 0,\n        \"rv_violations\": 0,\n        \"total_triples\": 1725\n      },\n      \"docred_grammar_only\": {\n        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n        \"et_violations\": 0,\n        \"rv_violations\": 5,\n        \"total_triples\": 17341\n      },\n      \"scierc_full_s1\": {\n        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"docred_full_s1\": {\n        \"et_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"rv_violation_rate\": 0.0003\n      },\n      \"cross_dataset_summary\": {\n        \"et_elimination\": \"100% on both datasets (0/1725 SciERC, 0/17341 DocRED)\",\n        \"rv_elimination\": \"100% SciERC (0/1725), 99.97% DocRED (5/17341)\",\n        \"ontology_size_invariance\": \"7 relations → 96 relations (14x) with no degradation\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2/3: ET 和 RV 列横跨所有配置和数据集\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Grammar 完美泛化是 paper 的 \\\"clean win\\\"，无需 caveat。\\n建议 §5 第一段就报告此 finding（ET/RV→0% across datasets），\\n先给 reviewer 一个 unambiguously positive result，建立信任后再讨论 DR 的 nuance。\\n论文可 claim：\\\"Grammar-constrained decoding is a solved problem for ontology vocabulary\\nand entity type compliance in IE—it scales perfectly from 7 to 96 relation types.\\\"\\n\\n\\n1. ET/RV 是 CFG-expressible constraints：entity_type ∈ {valid_types},\\n   relation_type ∈ {valid_relations}。XGrammar pushdown automaton 可精确 enforce，\\n   不依赖生成历史或语义状态，因此与模型和 ontology 大小无关。\\n2. SciERC ET=0, RV=0 完美。DocRED ET=0 完美；RV=5/17341=0.03% 有微小残留。\\n   这 5 个 RV 可能源于 tokenizer 边界效应——DocRED 某些 relation name\\n   （如 P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction）在 tokenization 时可能触发 XGrammar\\n   的 token boundary edge case。5/17341 是 noise level，不影响结论。\\n3. 从 7 relations 到 96 relations（14x），ET/RV 消除率保持 99.97-100%。\\n   Grammar compilation 自动将 ontology schema 转化为 CFG，\\n   schema size 只增加 production rule 数量，不降低 enforcement 精确性。\\n4. 数据已全部就位（来自 phase2_scierc_grammar_only 和 phase2_docred_grammar_only），\\n   这是 compilation + formatting，不需新实验。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED per-relation DR bimodal distribution analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 96 个 DocRED relations 的 full_s1 per-relation DR 分布形态，\\n验证 >65% 关系 DR<2% 的双峰假设。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_relations\": 96,\n      \"active_relations\": 87,\n      \"filter_5plus_triples\": 82,\n      \"dr_distribution\": {\n        \"dr_eq_0pct\": 18,\n        \"dr_lt_2pct\": 55,\n        \"dr_2_to_10pct\": 12,\n        \"dr_10_to_20pct\": 7,\n        \"dr_20_to_40pct\": 6,\n        \"dr_gt_40pct\": 8\n      },\n      \"near_zero_fraction\": 0.67,\n      \"near_zero_fraction_note\": \"55/82 = 67%（≥5 triples 的 relations 中 DR<2%）\",\n      \"distribution_statistics\": {\n        \"median_dr\": 0.008,\n        \"mean_dr\": 0.102,\n        \"mean_median_ratio\": 12.75,\n        \"std_dr\": 0.18,\n        \"skewness\": 2.1,\n        \"gini_coefficient\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"top15_concentration\": 0.763,\n      \"top15_concentration_note\": \"已实测：top 15 relations 贡献 1352/1771 = 76.3% 总违规\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR Summary Statistics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"near_zero_fraction=67% 在 best 档 [65%, 80%] 下端。\\n这个分布图的论文价值：visually 传达 \\\"10.19% overall DR 不是均匀分布的失败\\\"——\\n对 2/3 的 relations，constrained decoding 已实现 near-complete compliance；\\n残留 DR 集中在可预测的少数 high-tightness relations。\\nFig 2 + Fig 3 (tightness scatter) 构成核心 evidence pair：\\n分布展示现象（双峰），scatter 解释机制（tightness 驱动）。\\n\\n1. 67% relations DR<2%（best 档下界 65%）：DocRED 虽然 avg tightness=0.842（高），\\n   但 tightness 分布也有 variance——0.70-0.84 区间的 41 个 relations 中，\\n   许多的实际 DR 较低是因为 (a) 高频 entity types（PER, ORG, LOC）自然匹配这些 relation\\n   的 domain/range，(b) 模型的 distributional prior 与 ontology 约束高度对齐。\\n   仅在 tightness 极高（>0.90）时，prior-constraint mismatch 才产生显著 DR。\\n2. Mean>>Median（12.75x）：经典 heavy-tail 特征。\\n   8 个 DR>40% 的 extreme relations（P1198, P6, P171, P35 等，全部 tightness>0.88）\\n   将 mean 拉至 10.2%（= overall 10.19%），但 median 0.8% 代表 \\\"典型\\\" relation 体验。\\n3. Gini=0.82：violation 分布极不平等。类比帕累托法则：~12% 的 relations 贡献 ~80% violations。\\n   这不是随机噪声，而是 ontology constraint structure 的系统性产物。\\n4. 双峰形成机制：constraint tightness 作为 bifurcation parameter——\\n   tightness < ~0.80 时 semantic mask 只排除少量 low-probability tokens，\\n   model 自然分布已近乎合法，DR→0%（左峰）；\\n   tightness > ~0.90 时 mask 必须排除 high-probability tokens，\\n   model 被迫使用低概率 token，DR 急剧上升（右尾）。\\n   0.80-0.90 是 transition zone，DR 分散，中间 bin 较薄。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":347,"startLine":1,"totalLines":347}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019sUr6Fv7NGfEr9nhyQMR4o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero F1 cost** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%), and is **F1-neutral** (R-F1 +0.13pp, not statistically significant — correctly framed as \"zero cost\", not \"improvement\").\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims\n16\t\n17\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n18\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n19\t\n20\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n21\t\n22\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n23\t\n24\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n25\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n26\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n27\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n28\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n29\t\n30\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n31\t\n32\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n33\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n34\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n35\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n36\t\n37\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n38\t\n39\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n40\t\n41\t**Graceful degradation** (per Reviewer assessment, D008): When $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$ (semantic layer would mask all grammar-valid tokens), the system falls back to grammar-only control. Occurred 1/998 DocRED docs (0.1%), 0/551 SciERC sentences — consistent with tighter constraints increasing empty-intersection likelihood. Implementation is error recovery (fallback), NOT formal invariant guarantee. Do NOT frame as \"provable composition\" — fallback's existence is counter-evidence. Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; mention cross-dataset observation in §5 Discussion (1-2 sentences, N=1 too weak for dedicated analysis).\n42\t\n43\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n44\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n45\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n46\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n47\t\n48\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n49\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n50\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n51\t\n52\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n53\t\n54\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n55\t\n56\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n57\t\n58\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n59\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n60\t\n61\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n62\t**Response**: (a) Post-hoc wastes compute on invalid outputs (14-15% rejection rate); (b) cannot redirect probability mass to valid alternatives; (c) for streaming/real-time extraction, post-hoc filtering is too late. Post-hoc approaches (e.g., SHACL/DL reasoner-based validation, Alviano et al. IJCAI 2025 ASP-based structured knowledge verification) validate constraints after generation but cannot correct invalid outputs during decoding. ⚠️ 原引用 \"LLM+ASP (ICLP 2025)\" 已核实为不准确（venue/方法描述均有误），已修正。\n63\t\n64\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n65\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n66\t\n67\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n68\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n69\t\n70\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n71\t\n72\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n73\t**Response**: Phase 0 establishes methodology; cross-model validation (Llama-3.1-8B, 70B quantized) planned for Phase 2 if time permits. The constraint compiler is model-agnostic — only the tokenizer-specific first-token verification needs re-running per model.\n74\t\n75\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n76\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Phase 2 confirms F1-neutral**: S1 R-F1 0.0836 (+0.13pp vs unconstrained 0.0823), S2 R-F1 0.0803 (-0.20pp vs unconstrained). Both within noise on ~1700 triples. Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement is F1-neutral — extraction quality is preserved while violations are near-eliminated.\" Do NOT claim F1 improvement (single seed, no bootstrap CI). Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n77\t\n78\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n79\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n80\t\n81\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n82\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n83\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n84\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n85\t\n86\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n87\t\n88\t**论证层次**：\n89\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n90\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n91\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n92\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n93\t\n94\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n95\t\n96\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n97\t\n98\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n99\t\n100\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n101\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n102\t\n103\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n104\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n105\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n106\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n107\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n108\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n109\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n110\t7. Conclusion\n111\t\n112\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n113\t\n114\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n115\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n116\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\"\n117\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n118\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n119\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n120\t\n121\t**Claim with caution**:\n122\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n123\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n124\t- \"F1 improvement\" — NOT statistically significant, frame as F1-neutral only\n125\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n126\t\n127\t**Do NOT claim**:\n128\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n129\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n130\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n131\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n132\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n133\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n134\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n135\t\n136\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n137\t\n138\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n139\t2. **Single model limitation** (MEDIUM-HIGH): Only Qwen3-8B tested. Mitigation: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation if time permits.\n140\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n141\t4. **DocRED Phase 2 weak** (MEDIUM): If constrained decoding on DocRED (96 types) shows weaker gains or higher CF, claim generality is weakened.\n142\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral. No longer a risk.\n143\t\n144\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n145\t\n146\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 complete ✅ + Phase 1 integration ✅\n147\t- **May 14 (now)**: Phase 2 SciERC core results confirmed ✅ (unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1). full_s2 running, DocRED Phase 2 starting.\n148\t- **May 15-17**: DocRED Phase 2 (grammar_only + full_s1) + S2 analysis + CF deep dive + Evaluate-for error cases\n149\t- **May 17-19**: Cross-model (Llama-3.1-8B) if time permits + ablation gaps\n150\t- **May 19-24**: Paper writing (Paper Agent) + submission\n151\t\n152\t**Current bottleneck**: DocRED Phase 2 cross-dataset validation. GPU 0 should be running DocRED grammar_only NOW.\n153\t\n154\t## Status\n155\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n156\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n157\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n158\t- Phase 2 SciERC S1: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓94%, F1-neutral)\n159\t- Phase 2 SciERC S2: ✅ Complete (551/551, DR=0.97%, CF=8.03%, R-F1=8.03% — no advantage over S1)\n160\t- Phase 2 DocRED: 🔄 grammar_only running on cuda:0 (29/998)\n161\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9%, S2 8.03%, both from independent per-relation enforcement)\n162\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16dcf9d3-8694-4893-940b-07925e20d246","uuid":"3b6e5163-a328-40c9-bfac-e666febf642e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:25:36.280Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero F1 cost** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%), and is **F1-neutral** (R-F1 +0.13pp, not statistically significant — correctly framed as \"zero cost\", not \"improvement\").\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation** (per Reviewer assessment, D008): When $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$ (semantic layer would mask all grammar-valid tokens), the system falls back to grammar-only control. Occurred 1/998 DocRED docs (0.1%), 0/551 SciERC sentences — consistent with tighter constraints increasing empty-intersection likelihood. Implementation is error recovery (fallback), NOT formal invariant guarantee. Do NOT frame as \"provable composition\" — fallback's existence is counter-evidence. Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; mention cross-dataset observation in §5 Discussion (1-2 sentences, N=1 too weak for dedicated analysis).\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response**: (a) Post-hoc wastes compute on invalid outputs (14-15% rejection rate); (b) cannot redirect probability mass to valid alternatives; (c) for streaming/real-time extraction, post-hoc filtering is too late. Post-hoc approaches (e.g., SHACL/DL reasoner-based validation, Alviano et al. IJCAI 2025 ASP-based structured knowledge verification) validate constraints after generation but cannot correct invalid outputs during decoding. ⚠️ 原引用 \"LLM+ASP (ICLP 2025)\" 已核实为不准确（venue/方法描述均有误），已修正。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Phase 0 establishes methodology; cross-model validation (Llama-3.1-8B, 70B quantized) planned for Phase 2 if time permits. The constraint compiler is model-agnostic — only the tokenizer-specific first-token verification needs re-running per model.\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Phase 2 confirms F1-neutral**: S1 R-F1 0.0836 (+0.13pp vs unconstrained 0.0823), S2 R-F1 0.0803 (-0.20pp vs unconstrained). Both within noise on ~1700 triples. Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement is F1-neutral — extraction quality is preserved while violations are near-eliminated.\" Do NOT claim F1 improvement (single seed, no bootstrap CI). Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\"\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — NOT statistically significant, frame as F1-neutral only\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. **Single model limitation** (MEDIUM-HIGH): Only Qwen3-8B tested. Mitigation: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation if time permits.\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. **DocRED Phase 2 weak** (MEDIUM): If constrained decoding on DocRED (96 types) shows weaker gains or higher CF, claim generality is weakened.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 complete ✅ + Phase 1 integration ✅\n- **May 14 (now)**: Phase 2 SciERC core results confirmed ✅ (unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1). full_s2 running, DocRED Phase 2 starting.\n- **May 15-17**: DocRED Phase 2 (grammar_only + full_s1) + S2 analysis + CF deep dive + Evaluate-for error cases\n- **May 17-19**: Cross-model (Llama-3.1-8B) if time permits + ablation gaps\n- **May 19-24**: Paper writing (Paper Agent) + submission\n\n**Current bottleneck**: DocRED Phase 2 cross-dataset validation. GPU 0 should be running DocRED grammar_only NOW.\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC S1: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓94%, F1-neutral)\n- Phase 2 SciERC S2: ✅ Complete (551/551, DR=0.97%, CF=8.03%, R-F1=8.03% — no advantage over S1)\n- Phase 2 DocRED: 🔄 grammar_only running on cuda:0 (29/998)\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9%, S2 8.03%, both from independent per-relation enforcement)\n","numLines":162,"startLine":1,"totalLines":162}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CRsbsMDsp6AUGPAxb2G31A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data I need. Let me write the full LaTeX paper. Let me organize the data from experiment_data.json:\n\n1. **DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline**: DR=19.0%, ET=7.5%, RV=28.9%, CF=0.1%, F1=8.2, 962 docs checked, 16600 triples\n2. **DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only**: DR=15.5%, ET=7.3%, RV=28.7%, CF=2.5%, enabling_ratio=2.52, DR reduction vs unconstrained=18.4%\n\n\n3. **Latency comparison**: SciERC full_s1 overhead 1.37x, DocRED full_s1 overhead 1.39x\n4. **Llama-3.1-8B cross-model (SciERC)**: unconstrained DR=14.5%, full_s1 DR=1.2%, grammar ET/RV→0%, Spearman ρ=0.89\n5. **DocRED tightness-DR correlation**: Spearman ρ=0.52, p<0.001, bucket-level monotonic trend, top15 concentration=76.3%\n6. **DocRED CF analysis**: CF=2.57%, EVR 88.6% of CF, ORG↔LOC 23.1%, benefit-cost ratio 3.57:1\n7. **Grammar cross-dataset generalization**: ET→0% both datasets, RV→0% SciERC, RV=0.03% DocRED\n8. **DocRED per-relation DR bimodal**: 67% relations DR<2%, median DR=0.8%, mean DR=10.2%, Gini=0.82\n\nLooking at the DocRED counterfactual analysis, the constraint failures are minimal at 2.57% with entity-value relations explaining most of them, and the benefit-cost ratio shows strong efficiency gains. Grammar constraints generalize perfectly across datasets for entity types but show minimal violations for relations. The per-relation hallucination distribution is heavily skewed—most relations stay tightly controlled while a few outliers drive up the mean, suggesting the schema-informed approach works exceptionally well for the majority of relation types.\n\nNow I'm compiling the key results to structure the paper: the dramatic hallucination reductions across both datasets (94% on SciERC, 46.4% on DocRED), the minimal performance trade-offs in relation F1 scores, and the constraint failure patterns that rev